# Keeps recycler views marked with `item.virtualSticky` alive.
#
# Memories sets `virtualSticky = true` on the touched row during touch-hold
# selection (see SelectionManager::touchstartPhoto). The view backing that row
# must stay in the DOM for the whole gesture, otherwise the browser stops
# delivering touchmove/touchend events and the drag selection breaks.
# This ports the old vue-virtual-scroller v1 patch to the v3 codebase, which
# has TWO places that release views (v1 had one):
#   1. the visible-range keep-check in updateVisibleItems: sticky views are
#      treated as in range so they are never released;
#   2. the Kt() full reset (runs when the item keys change, e.g. rows are
#      added while auto-scroll loads more days): sticky views are skipped and
#      stay registered in the key map so the render loop reuses them in place
#      instead of mounting duplicates.
#
